message.content:
This is likely a CBP ruling on side mount electrical conductor assemblies for EV battery modules. Candidates are 8544.42 / 8544.49 (insulated electric conductors) and 8536.90 (connectors) or 8536.90.40/8536.90.85. A part with an aluminum bus bar in a molded housing is also covered by 8548 or 8507.90 (parts of batteries).

I recall CBP ruling N319... on "busbar assemblies" for EV battery: classified in 8544.42.9090 (other electric conductors, for a voltage not exceeding 1,000 V, fitted with connectors). Other rulings classify bus bars with insulated housings in 8536.90.8585 or 8538.90. A conductor bar enclosed in an insulating housing is an insulated conductor, and an assembly with connector configurations fits 8544.42. With a voltage above 80 V but not above 1,000 V, the code is 8544.42.90 with statistical suffix 90. Since aluminum bar is "other conductors," I'll go with 8544.42.9090.

{"hts_code": "8544.42.9090", "reason": "The aluminum conductor bar in an insulating polyamide 66 housing with connector configurations is an insulated electric conductor fitted with connectors, for a voltage not exceeding 1,000 V, so it falls under heading 8544 (8544.42)."}
